Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.270 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  kendall jenner brought in her 25th  birthday  early with a halloween themed party  the supermodel whose birthday is on  tuesday  hosted her celebration at harriet's  rooftop a top one hotel  in west hollywood  the party's star-studded guest list  included her sister  kylie jenner dosiacat sweetie  travis scott cuevo justin bieber  hailey bieber and the weeknd  name a few it's really awesome to be  able to share that with them  kim kardashian and kanye west also  joined in  on the festivities as well as family  friend  paris hilton e.t has learned that  every person who entered the venue both  employees  and party guests had to have a rapid  covet 19  test with a negative result on site  before going upstairs to the party  [Music]  the stars didn't come to play when it  comes to their costumes  kendall set the bar high stunning as  pamela anderson  from barbwire dosiacats served  fierceness  as tyra banks and the weeknd spent  six hours getting into his nutty  professor  costume  despite the good time the guests had the  party hasn't been well received by users  on social media fans were quick to voice  concerns  about a lack of social distancing and  mask  this comes soon after her sister kim  kardashian  also received some criticism for the  pictures and  captions she shared of her 40th birthday  private island celebration fans accused  the reality star's post  of being tone deaf and insensitive to  those suffering right now  amid the global pandemic kim's close  friend  lala anthony who attended the  celebration recently shared her thoughts  on the backlash  to e.t i don't really think too much  about it i just know we live in a world  where  people are going to have something to  say about everything it's just  what it is there's something that's  going to be said about everything you  wear a black top you should have wore a  red one you wear a blue top why didn't  you wear  the black one it's just the world we  live in and i don't really get you know  too caught up in that i know what we're  all doing individually when it comes to  charities when it comes to using our  platforms when it comes to voting  when it comes to prison reform when it  comes to the millions of things that  we're doing to try to you know just  help the world in general and that's  what what matters to me it's not just  about  going on an island and taking a  beautiful picture i mean there's a lot  more  to what all of us do in our day-to-day  lives you know than that and that's  that's what matters i rather amplify  that side of what we're doing

